 ```
 
+##### limit
+
+Specifies the maximum number of ranges to return from one header, unset (no
+limit) by default. Must be a positive integer, otherwise a `TypeError` is
+thrown. Only valid, satisfiable ranges are counted, and if `combine` is `true`
+they are counted after combining. When there are more ranges than the limit,
+they are merged into a single range from the lowest start to the highest end.
+Note this includes the bytes in the gaps between the original ranges.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(1000, 'bytes=0-10,500-510,900-910', { limit: 2 })
+// => [
+//      { start: 0, end: 910 }
+//    ]
+```
+
